('bab43eca-f2c2-529b-8d2f-ab84fc5dc422'::uuid,'est2','"Functions, Transformations & Graphs"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"[Figure: \"Student''s Workout\" — line from (0, 100) to (50, 0); y = percentage remaining, x = minutes.]\nA student worked out at a gym continuously for 50 minutes. The graph shows the remaining percentage of the workout as a linear function of x, the time in minutes. Which answer choice best describes the domain and range of the function for this situation?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"Domain: all real numbers ≥ 0 and ≤ 100; Range: all real numbers ≥ 0 and ≤ 50"},{"key":"B","text":"Domain: {−2}; Range: {100}"},{"key":"C","text":"Domain: all real numbers ≥ 0 and ≤ 50; Range: all real numbers ≥ 0 and ≤ 100"},{"key":"D","text":"Domain: {100}; Range: {−2}"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t8.md","source_sha256":"8f03df34fa98881a0531e925df7d2a108b1590182b68af8e273abe0930b44cfb","source_question_id":"T8-11","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Functions, Transformations & Graphs"}'::jsonb,'"C"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t8.md (T8-11)."'::jsonb),
('fb4887b7-a059-5cd4-931f-dd912ed84086'::uuid,'est2','"Coordinate Geometry, Circles & Conics"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"[Figure: four parabolas. F: vertex (−2, 5). G: vertex (2, −5). H: vertex (−2, −5). J: vertex (2, 5).]\nThe graph of quadratic parent function f was transformed to create the graph of g(x) = f(x + 2) − 5. Which graph best represents g?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"F","text":"Graph F"},{"key":"G","text":"Graph G"},{"key":"H","text":"Graph H"},{"key":"J","text":"Graph J"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t8.md","source_sha256":"8f03df34fa98881a0531e925df7d2a108b1590182b68af8e273abe0930b44cfb","source_question_id":"T8-12","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Coordinate Geometry, Circles & Conics"}'::jsonb,'"H"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t8.md (T8-12)."'::jsonb),
('9d80b5dc-c770-557c-b16c-0b4697a0c1c8'::uuid,'est2','"Rational, Radical, Exponential & Logarithmic Functions"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"Which expression is equivalent to (45m⁻⁶p²v¹²)/(15m⁻²p⁸v⁻⁴) for all values of m, p, and v where the expression is defined?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"3v⁸/(m⁸p⁶)"},{"key":"B","text":"3v¹⁶/(m⁴p⁶)"},{"key":"C","text":"30m³/(p⁴v³)"},{"key":"D","text":"30v³/(m³p⁴)"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t8.md","source_sha256":"8f03df34fa98881a0531e925df7d2a108b1590182b68af8e273abe0930b44cfb","source_question_id":"T8-13","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Rational, Radical, Exponential & Logarithmic Functions"}'::jsonb,'"B"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t8.md (T8-13)."'::jsonb),
('dc2a797b-89f4-5c90-8692-770c59844a08'::uuid,'est2','"Solid Geometry & Volume"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"[Figure: Sphere with diameter 15 in. marked across the center.]\nA sphere and its dimension are shown in the diagram. Which measurement is closest to the volume of the sphere in cubic inches?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"F","text":"1,325.4 in.³"},{"key":"G","text":"188.5 in.³"},{"key":"H","text":"94.2 in.³"},{"key":"J","text":"1,767.1 in.³"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t8.md","source_sha256":"8f03df34fa98881a0531e925df7d2a108b1590182b68af8e273abe0930b44cfb","source_question_id":"T8-14","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Solid Geometry & Volume"}'::jsonb,'"J"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t8.md (T8-14)."'::jsonb),
('8f8d4b04-4f8c-5809-a452-b3c1d3ba5155'::uuid,'est2','"Polynomials & Quadratic Functions"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"Which expression is equivalent to (10 + 7r − r²) + (−6r² − 18 + 5r)?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"F","text":"−7r² + 2r + 8"},{"key":"G","text":"7r² + 12r + 8"},{"key":"H","text":"−7r² + 12r − 8"},{"key":"J","text":"7r² + 2r − 8"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t8.md","source_sha256":"8f03df34fa98881a0531e925df7d2a108b1590182b68af8e273abe0930b44cfb","source_question_id":"T8-15","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Polynomials & Quadratic Functions"}'::jsonb,'"B"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t8.md (T8-15)."'::jsonb),
('f4623983-7dab-5b95-bf5f-1b8053d817d3'::uuid,'est2','"Solid Geometry & Volume"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"Which graph best represents the solution set of y > 3x − 4?\n[Figure: four grids. A: solid line slope 3 through (0,−4), shaded below-right. B: solid line slope 3, shaded above. C: dashed line slope 3, shaded below. D: dashed line slope 3 through (0,−4), shaded above.]"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"Graph A"},{"key":"B","text":"Graph B"},{"key":"C","text":"Graph C"},{"key":"D","text":"Graph D"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t8.md","source_sha256":"8f03df34fa98881a0531e925df7d2a108b1590182b68af8e273abe0930b44cfb","source_question_id":"T8-17","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Solid Geometry & Volume"}'::jsonb,'"D"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t8.md (T8-17)."'::jsonb),
('d1f66e14-ce4d-5515-bdcf-11f5a31eb25d'::uuid,'est2','"Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis"'::jsonb,'easy','mcq','"A bank account earning annual compound interest was opened, and no additional deposits or withdrawals were made after the initial deposit. The balance in the account after x years can be modeled by b(x) = 850(1.025)ˣ. Which statement is the best interpretation of one of the values in this function?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"F","text":"The initial balance of the account decreases at a rate of 97.5% each year."},{"key":"G","text":"The balance in the account increases at a rate of 2.5% each year."},{"key":"H","text":"The initial balance of the account was $1,025."},{"key":"J","text":"The balance in the account at the end of one year is $850."}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t8.md","source_sha256":"8f03df34fa98881a0531e925df7d2a108b1590182b68af8e273abe0930b44cfb","source_question_id":"T8-18","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis"}'::jsonb,'"G"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t8.md (T8-18)."'::jsonb),
('3f5f34fc-e911-59fe-b0fd-30b646c48273'::uuid,'est2','"Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis"'::jsonb,'easy','mcq','"A company collected data for the number of text messages sent and received using a text-message application since October 2011. The table shows the number of text messages sent and received in billions over time. The data can be modeled by a quadratic function.\nMonths since Oct 2011, t: 5, 10, 15, 20, 25, 30, 35, 40\nMessages n(t) (billions): 3, 10, 17, 27, 44, 64, 86, 112\nWhich function best models the data?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"n(t) = −0.002t² + 0.55t + 5.02"},{"key":"B","text":"n(t) = 0.072t² − 0.15t + 2.73"},{"key":"C","text":"n(t) = −0.002t² + 5.02"},{"key":"D","text":"n(t) = 0.072t² + 2.73"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t8.md","source_sha256":"8f03df34fa98881a0531e925df7d2a108b1590182b68af8e273abe0930b44cfb","source_question_id":"T8-19","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis"}'::jsonb,'"B"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t8.md (T8-19)."'::jsonb),
('1303e528-b2d3-5e94-a5d9-53f700821027'::uuid,'est2','"Triangles, Trigonometry & Similarity"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"[Figure: Two similar hexagons. Figure I: vertices R, S, T, U, V, W (R marked with double arc, T and V with single arcs). Figure II: vertices A, B, C, D, E, F (F single arc, B single arc, D double arc).]\nFigure I and Figure II are similar figures. Which proportion must be true?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"F","text":"RS/AB = TU/CD"},{"key":"G","text":"TU/AB = UV/AF"},{"key":"H","text":"ST/EF = WR/CD"},{"key":"J","text":"WV/AB = ST/EF"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t8.md","source_sha256":"8f03df34fa98881a0531e925df7d2a108b1590182b68af8e273abe0930b44cfb","source_question_id":"T8-20","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Triangles, Trigonometry & Similarity"}'::jsonb,'"H"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t8.md (T8-20)."'::jsonb),
('d8893501-dcc6-5773-b9af-58fb76a170b4'::uuid,'est2','"Coordinate Geometry, Circles & Conics"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"Which graph best represents y = −x² + 6x − 1?\n[Figure: four grids. A: parabola opening down, vertex (3, 8). B: parabola opening up, vertex (−3, −10)-ish. C: parabola opening up, vertex (−3,…) left of y-axis. D: parabola opening down, vertex left of y-axis.]"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"Graph A"},{"key":"B","text":"Graph B"},{"key":"C","text":"Graph C"},{"key":"D","text":"Graph D"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t8.md","source_sha256":"8f03df34fa98881a0531e925df7d2a108b1590182b68af8e273abe0930b44cfb","source_question_id":"T8-21","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Coordinate Geometry, Circles & Conics"}'::jsonb,'"A"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t8.md (T8-21)."'::jsonb),
('53ec0374-0ed3-5e48-a010-f556c151f99a'::uuid,'est2','"Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis"'::jsonb,'easy','mcq','"A company advertises on a website. A worker tracked the number of visits to the website and the number of clicks on the advertisement. The table shows the data for several days. A linear function can be used to model the data.\nVisits x: 153, 629, 471, 914, 307, 1045, 510, 1106\nClicks y: 14, 38, 30, 53, 21, 60, 32, 63\nBased on the table, what is the best prediction of the number of clicks on the advertisement if 1,500 people visit the website?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"F","text":"77"},{"key":"G","text":"137"},{"key":"H","text":"83"},{"key":"J","text":"105"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t8.md","source_sha256":"8f03df34fa98881a0531e925df7d2a108b1590182b68af8e273abe0930b44cfb","source_question_id":"T8-22","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis"}'::jsonb,'"H"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t8.md (T8-22)."'::jsonb),
('f1871874-be8c-5fc4-90c4-005cb8294756'::uuid,'est2','"Coordinate Geometry, Circles & Conics"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"[Figure: Line rising to the right, passing through (−3, −2) and (4, 3) approximately — slope 5/7, through (7, 2).]\nThe graph of a linear function is shown on the grid. Which equation is best represented by this graph?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"y + 2 = (7/5)(x + 7)"},{"key":"B","text":"y − 2 = (7/5)(x − 7)"},{"key":"C","text":"y + 2 = (5/7)(x + 7)"},{"key":"D","text":"y − 2 = (5/7)(x − 7)"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t8.md","source_sha256":"8f03df34fa98881a0531e925df7d2a108b1590182b68af8e273abe0930b44cfb","source_question_id":"T8-23","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Coordinate Geometry, Circles & Conics"}'::jsonb,'"D"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t8.md (T8-23)."'::jsonb),
