('b10c5ee4-2eb5-5490-86b6-30d02c7ee7e8'::uuid,'est2','"Polynomials & Quadratic Functions"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"Which expression is equivalent to 24x² − 22x + 5?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"(12x + 5)(2x + 1)"},{"key":"B","text":"(8x − 5)(3x − 1)"},{"key":"C","text":"(12x − 5)(2x − 1)"},{"key":"D","text":"(8x + 5)(3x + 1)"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t8.md","source_sha256":"8f03df34fa98881a0531e925df7d2a108b1590182b68af8e273abe0930b44cfb","source_question_id":"T8-29","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Polynomials & Quadratic Functions"}'::jsonb,'"C"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t8.md (T8-29)."'::jsonb),
('3fc89d2f-59c2-5575-828d-cfe0305e7d57'::uuid,'est2','"Functions, Transformations & Graphs"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"[Figure: Two lines on a grid: one falling through (−4, 4) and (−1, −2); one rising through (−1, 3) and (1, 5).]\nA system of equations is graphed on the grid. Which system of equations does the graph represent?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"F","text":"y = −x − 4; y = 2x − 2"},{"key":"G","text":"y = −x + 4; y = 2x − 4"},{"key":"H","text":"y = x − 4; y = −2x − 2"},{"key":"J","text":"y = x + 4; y = −2x − 4"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t8.md","source_sha256":"8f03df34fa98881a0531e925df7d2a108b1590182b68af8e273abe0930b44cfb","source_question_id":"T8-30","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Functions, Transformations & Graphs"}'::jsonb,'"J"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t8.md (T8-30)."'::jsonb),
('230e2424-0e5b-5917-8a2e-bdcad6453c5e'::uuid,'est2','"Rational, Radical, Exponential & Logarithmic Functions"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"The table represents some points on the graph of an exponential function.\nx: −2, −1, 0, 1, 2\nf(x): 12.5, 15, 18, 21.6, 25.92\nWhich function represents the same relationship?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"f(x) = 15(5/6)ˣ"},{"key":"B","text":"f(x) = 18(6/5)ˣ"},{"key":"C","text":"f(x) = 15(6/5)ˣ"},{"key":"D","text":"f(x) = 18(5/6)ˣ"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t8.md","source_sha256":"8f03df34fa98881a0531e925df7d2a108b1590182b68af8e273abe0930b44cfb","source_question_id":"T8-31","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Rational, Radical, Exponential & Logarithmic Functions"}'::jsonb,'"B"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t8.md (T8-31)."'::jsonb),
('b7959027-6a89-5cc8-ad01-01bdfe1ed6ab'::uuid,'est2','"Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis"'::jsonb,'easy','mcq','"The table shows the amount of pet food in cups remaining in an automatic feeder as a function of the number of meals the feeder has dispensed.\nMeals dispensed n: 1, 3, 6, 7\nCups remaining f(n): 21, 15, 6, 3\nBased on the table, which function models this situation?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"F","text":"f(n) = −3n + 24"},{"key":"G","text":"f(n) = −(1/3)n + 16"},{"key":"H","text":"f(n) = −3n + 64"},{"key":"J","text":"f(n) = −(1/3)n + 8"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t8.md","source_sha256":"8f03df34fa98881a0531e925df7d2a108b1590182b68af8e273abe0930b44cfb","source_question_id":"T8-32","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis"}'::jsonb,'"F"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t8.md (T8-32)."'::jsonb),
('ff7445b6-598a-53c8-b3d5-8d2d1496bb0d'::uuid,'est2','"Plane Geometry, Measurement & Transformations"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"The graph of f(x) = x² was transformed to create the graph of g(x) = f(x) − 9. Which statement about the graphs is true?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"The graph of g is a reflection of the graph of f across the x-axis."},{"key":"B","text":"The vertex of the graph of g is 9 units to the right of the vertex of the graph of f."},{"key":"C","text":"The graph of g is a reflection of the graph of f across the y-axis."},{"key":"D","text":"The y-intercept of the graph of g is 9 units below the y-intercept of the graph of f."}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t8.md","source_sha256":"8f03df34fa98881a0531e925df7d2a108b1590182b68af8e273abe0930b44cfb","source_question_id":"T8-33","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Plane Geometry, Measurement & Transformations"}'::jsonb,'"D"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t8.md (T8-33)."'::jsonb),
('15210e4e-fb7d-5227-86a2-a383e91a380c'::uuid,'est2','"Solid Geometry & Volume"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"[Figure: Cylinder (silo) with diameter 6.5 m and height 12 m.]\nA silo is a building shaped like a cylinder used to store grain. The diameter of a particular silo is 6.5 meters, and the height of the silo is 12 meters. Which equation can be used to find V, the volume of this silo in cubic meters?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"V = π(3.25)²(12)"},{"key":"B","text":"V = π(6.5)²(12)"},{"key":"C","text":"V = π(12)²(3.25)"},{"key":"D","text":"V = π(6)²(6.5)"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t8.md","source_sha256":"8f03df34fa98881a0531e925df7d2a108b1590182b68af8e273abe0930b44cfb","source_question_id":"T8-34","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Solid Geometry & Volume"}'::jsonb,'"A"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t8.md (T8-34)."'::jsonb),
